THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

MaMaDroid's own source imports the Python standard library plus these packages.
Nothing is vendored.

  numpy          - BSD-3-Clause - https://numpy.org/
  networkx       - BSD-3-Clause - https://networkx.org/
  androguard     - Apache-2.0   - https://github.com/androguard/androguard
  python-igraph  - GPL-2.0-or-later - https://igraph.org/python/

  NOTE on python-igraph: it is GPL-2.0-or-later. It is imported as a normal
  Python dependency, not vendored or linked into a binary, so this repository's
  own code is not thereby placed under the GPL. Distributing a combined work
  that includes igraph would be a different question - which is one reason this
  artefact is licensed as non-redistributable.

External tools invoked as subprocesses, never bundled:

  apktool  - Apache-2.0 - used by the APK → call-graph stage.
  Java/JVM - the androguard/dex2jar path needs a JRE on PATH.

Development only (not shipped, not imported at runtime):

  pytest   - MIT
  ruff     - MIT
  pyflakes - MIT

No third-party source code is vendored in this repository.
